{
  "problem": {
    "title": "Project Scheduling LP: Minimize Duration and Machine Rental Cost",
    "description": "A project has 7 activities (A through G) with fixed durations: A=4, B=3, C=5, D=2, E=10, F=10, G=1 days. Precedence constraints: A must finish before G and D start; E and G must finish before F starts; D and F must finish before C starts; F must finish before B starts. A machine is rented from the start of activity A until the end of activity B (duration = start_B + 3 - start_A days). Total project duration T = max finish time across all activities. Minimize cost = 1000*T + 5000*machine_days.",
    "problem_type": "linear_programming",
    "objective": "minimize",
    "objective_description": "Total cost = 1000 * T + 5000 * machine_days",
    "constraints": [
      {
        "description": "Precedence A->G: t_G >= t_A + 4"
      },
      {
        "description": "Precedence A->D: t_D >= t_A + 4"
      },
      {
        "description": "Precedence E->F: t_F >= t_E + 10"
      },
      {
        "description": "Precedence G->F: t_F >= t_G + 1"
      },
      {
        "description": "Precedence D->C: t_C >= t_D + 2"
      },
      {
        "description": "Precedence F->C: t_C >= t_F + 10"
      },
      {
        "description": "Precedence F->B: t_B >= t_F + 10"
      },
      {
        "description": "T >= finish time of each activity (7 constraints)"
      },
      {
        "description": "machine_days = t_B + 3 - t_A"
      }
    ],
    "decision_variables": [
      "t_A, t_B, t_C, t_D, t_E, t_F, t_G: start times of each activity (scalar continuous, non-negative)",
      "T: total project duration (scalar continuous, non-negative)",
      "machine_days: days the machine is rented (scalar continuous, non-negative)"
    ],
    "parameters": [],
    "additional_notes": "All constraints use domain=[] (scalar). No sets or parameters needed; all data is hardcoded as constants. Optimal: t_A=0, t_E=0, t_G=4, t_D=4, t_F=14, t_C=24, t_B=24, T=27, machine_days=27. Wait - let me recheck. t_F >= t_G+1=5 and t_F >= t_E+10=10, so t_F=10 if t_E=0 and t_G=4. Then t_B>=t_F+10=20, t_C>=max(t_D+2,t_F+10)=max(6,20)=20. So T>=max(t_A+4,t_B+3,t_C+5,t_D+2,t_E+10,t_F+10,t_G+1)=max(4,23,25,6,10,20,5)=25. machine_days=t_B+3-t_A=20+3-0=23. Obj=1000*25+5000*23=25000+115000=140000. Actually expected is 115000: T=25, machine=18. Recheck: if t_A=5, t_E=0, t_G=9, t_D=9, t_F=10, t_B=20, T=25 (from t_B+3=23... no). Let me re-examine. If t_A can start later, t_E=0, t_F=10, t_B=20, T=max(t_B+3,t_C+5,...)=23 if t_C=18. machine_days=t_B+3-t_A=23-t_A. To minimize: push t_A as late as possible. t_A needs t_G=t_A+4 and t_F>=t_G+1=t_A+5, but t_F=10 is fixed by E path. So t_A+5<=10 => t_A<=5. With t_A=5: t_G=9, t_F>=max(10,10)=10, t_D=9, t_C>=max(11,20)=20, t_B>=20, T=max(9,23,25,11,10,20,10)=25. machine_days=23-5=18. Obj=25000+90000=115000. Correct!",
    "csv_file_paths": {}
  },
